    "body": "## Summary\n- require an authenticated ADMIN principal inside `DisputeService.getAdminDisputes`\n- pass the authenticated admin from `AdminDisputeController`\n- add regression coverage proving USER/null callers fail before repository access while ADMIN remains allowed\n- document the service-level authorization invariant for sensitive admin queues/evidence/financial state\n\n## Why this is launch-blocking P1\nThe HTTP route is already protected by `/admin/**.hasRole(\"ADMIN\")`, but the dispute queue service itself previously trusted that routing boundary. That made an especially sensitive moderation/financial queue vulnerable to future alternate call paths or refactors that bypass URL-level authorization. Other dispute admin operations already validate the admin principal in the service, so this closes that inconsistent boundary fail-closed.\n\n## Validation\nExact PR head checks must all pass before merge. Do not merge on pending/failing checks or if `master` moves without safely updating this branch.",
